fact WorkItem(id: "WI-1007", description: some(value: "SCALAND: THE LOADER'S WHOLE EXPRESSION-CONVERSION CLUSTER IS UNREACHABLE — ~250 LINES, NO CALLER. `Loader.convertExprTerm` (load/Loader.scala) has exactly ONE reference in the tree besides its own definition: `exprRec`, five lines below it. `exprRec`'s callers are the twelve `load*Expr`/`load*Pattern` helpers, and every one of THOSE is called only from `convertExprTerm`'s own by-name dispatch. It is a closed loop with no external entry — as are `buildList`/`buildSome`/`buildNone`, whose only callers are inside it. MEASURED: deleting the block leaves `core/compile` clean, and `sbt test` is unaffected. The live path is `reallocTerm`, which `LoadPass` calls for facts and rule heads and which never dispatches into this cluster; `ExprLoaderTest` says so in a comment ('facts use reallocTerm, not convertExprTerm'). WHY IT MATTERS beyond line count: it is not inert. WI-1004 spent its most intricate new construct on it (the `Ctx` class, threading `kb.ScopeId` through 14 signatures) before the deadness was noticed, and WI-957/WI-989's span work threads through it too — every future change to the loader's types pays a tax here for code nothing runs. WORK: settle what it IS first, because that decides delete-vs-keep and the answer is not in the code. Two candidates: (a) a port-ahead seam mirroring rustland's `convert_expr_term`, written before scaland had anything to consume Expr terms — scaland has no typer and no evaluator, and `Item.OperationItem` deliberately loads no body ('the declared type + optional body are not loaded', DefinePass's `ConstItem` arm says the same); or (b) a caller that was removed and took the entry point with it — check the history of `LoadPass.atItem` and of `reallocTerm`'s `Term.Fn` arm. If (a), the honest form is a LOUD refusal at the one place a body would enter, not 250 lines of unexercised machinery kept warm; if (b), restoring the caller is the fix and the cluster needs tests that DRIVE it. Either way do not leave it as is. ACCEPTANCE: scaland-sbt-test green, and either the cluster is gone or a test resolves a goal that reaches `convertExprTerm` and asserts the Expr term it built — 'it compiles' is not evidence. Found by code review of WI-1004 (2026-08-05). Related: WI-1004, WI-957."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "scaland-sbt-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-08-05T04:35:29Z"))

